<title>TURKEY: Turk cen bank reserves fell $306 mln last week.</title>
<headline>Turk cen bank reserves fell $306 mln last week.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves fell by $306 million to $15.943 billion in the week ending on September 20.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>		   Sept 20	Sept 13	end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve  15.943	 16.249	  12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve    1.383	  1.383	   1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve  17.326	 17.632	  13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose by $390 million to $27.848 billion in the week ending September 6, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
